Description: find DMARC reports pointed at expired (unregistered) domains
 rua-tool inspects the DMARC record published at _dmarc.<domain> and checks the
 domains that its aggregate (rua) and forensic (ruf) reports are sent to. If a
 report address points at a registrable domain that is unregistered or about to
 expire, an attacker could register it and begin receiving that organisation's
 DMARC reports, leaking mail infrastructure and aiding spoofing.
 .
 The tool can check a single domain, spider a site to harvest and scan many
 domains, discover a responsible-disclosure contact, and draft notices for the
 affected webmasters. All lookups are read-only (DNS, RDAP, HTTP GET) and it
 never sends mail.
